{
  "summary": "Report -rpcwhitelist denials as structured JSON-RPC errors instead of empty HTTP 403 responses. Introduce error codes RPC_METHOD_NOT_PERMITTED (-38) for refused method calls and RPC_REQUEST_NOT_EXECUTED (-39) for unexecuted calls in a rejected batch. Return HTTP 200 with an error object or array for JSON-RPC 2.0 and batch requests, while retaining HTTP 403 with an error payload for legacy 1.x requests.",
  "problem": "Requests refused by -rpcwhitelist return an empty HTTP 403 body. This violates documented JSON-RPC 2.0 behavior (which requires errors in HTTP 200 response bodies), causes bitcoin-cli over HTTP to show an uninformative 403 message, and breaks bitcoin-cli over IPC (-ipcconnect) with JSON type decoding errors because IPC receives only the body without HTTP status codes.",
  "evidence": [
    "Identified in a private security audit of the IPC interface (ar-56) where bitcoin-cli -ipcconnect fails with a JSON type error on rejected calls.",
    "Brings -rpcwhitelist error handling in line with JSON-RPC 2.0 behavior documented in #27101 and doc/JSON-RPC-interface.md."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Modifies HTTP RPC processing in src/httprpc.cpp and adds two RPCErrorCode enum entries in src/rpc/protocol.h.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Diff provided; no changes to commits or design relative to the previous version.",
  "card": "Bitcoin Core currently returns an empty HTTP 403 response when requests are refused by -rpcwhitelist, which leaves HTTP clients with vague errors and breaks bitcoin-cli over IPC with JSON decoding errors. This PR changes whitelist refusals to return standard JSON-RPC errors in the response body using new error codes RPC_METHOD_NOT_PERMITTED (-38) and RPC_REQUEST_NOT_EXECUTED (-39). JSON-RPC 2.0 single and batch requests now receive HTTP 200 responses with structured error objects, matching existing JSON-RPC 2.0 specifications. The defect was surfaced during a security audit of the IPC interface.",
